        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Black spinel, called pleonaste or ceylonite, is an iron-rich variety of spinel, between magnesian spinel and hercynite. It crystallises in marbles and skarns formed at the contact with magmas, in aluminium- and iron-rich metamorphic rocks, and in basalts and mantle peridotites, from which it was brought up as xenoliths. Resistant to erosion, it concentrates in gem gravels with sapphire, zircon and garnet. The abundant iron absorbs all light and makes it opaque in ordinary light, with a lively lustre.",
